# Beszel hub<->agent pairing (one-time, from the hub's "Add System" dialog on first run).
# Gitignored as beszel/.env. Both values come from the same dialog.
#
# 1. Bring the stack up: docker compose -f beszel/docker-compose.yml up -d
# 2. Open https://beszel.home.lan, log in, click "Add System".
# 3. Choose "Docker", Name = anything, Host/IP = beszel-agent, Port = 45876.
# 4. Copy the shown public KEY and TOKEN into beszel/.env below.
# 5. docker compose -f beszel/docker-compose.yml up -d --force-recreate beszel-agent
# 6. Save the system in the dialog — it connects (hub -> agent over the beszel network).
BESZEL_KEY=ssh-ed25519 AAAA...paste-hub-public-key-here...
BESZEL_TOKEN=paste-token-here
